{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SQLiteKit\/documentation\/SQLiteKit\/ExecutingSQL","doc:\/\/SQLiteKit\/documentation\/SQLiteKit\/SchemaManagement","doc:\/\/SQLiteKit\/documentation\/SQLiteKit\/MappingRows"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Add SQLiteKit","level":2,"anchor":"Add-SQLiteKit","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the package to another Swift package or Xcode project and import the library target:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import SQLiteKit"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"SQLiteKit supports macOS 14, iOS 17, tvOS 17, watchOS 10, visionOS 1, and newer platform versions declared by the package.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Open a Database","level":2,"anchor":"Open-a-Database","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SQLiteKit\/documentation\/SQLiteKit\/SQLiteDatabase","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" with a file path:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let database = try SQLiteDatabase(path: \"\/tmp\/app.sqlite\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For temporary or unit-test use, open an in-memory database:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let database = try SQLiteDatabase(path: \":memory:\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"During initialization SQLiteKit configures the connection with these defaults:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"PRAGMA synchronous = NORMAL","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PRAGMA temp_store = MEMORY"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can tune the connection at open time:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let database = try SQLiteDatabase(","    path: \"\/tmp\/app.sqlite\",","    tempStore: .memory,","    synchronous: .full,","    cacheSize: -20_000,","    mmapSize: 256 * 1024 * 1024",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SQLite follows "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PRAGMA cache_size"},{"text":" semantics. A positive ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cacheSize"},{"type":"text","text":" is interpreted as a number of database pages. A negative "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cacheSize"},{"type":"text","text":" is interpreted as an approximate size in kibibytes, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-20_000"},{"type":"text","text":" requests about 20,000 KiB of page cache."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Actor Isolation","level":2,"anchor":"Actor-Isolation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SQLiteKit\/documentation\/SQLiteKit\/SQLiteDatabase","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is an actor. Calls from outside the actor use ","type":"text"},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"code":["try await database.execute {","    \"CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS users(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL);\"","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Actor isolation serializes access to the underlying SQLite connection."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Create-a-Schema","level":2,"text":"Create a Schema"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SQLiteKit\/documentation\/SQLiteKit\/SQLiteDatabase\/schema(mode:entities:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" to declare the desired schema:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["try await database.schema {","    Table(name: \"users\")","        .column(name: \"id\", type: \"INTEGER\", notNull: true)","        .column(name: \"name\", type: \"TEXT\", notNull: true)","        .column(name: \"created_at\", type: \"TEXT\", defaultValue: \"CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\")","        .primaryKey(name: \"pk_users\", columns: [\"id\"])","        .index(name: \"idx_users_name\", columns: [\"name\"])","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If a table is missing, SQLiteKit creates it. If a supported schema difference is detected, SQLiteKit rebuilds the table and copies data into the replacement table.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Insert-Data","type":"heading","text":"Insert Data"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use raw SQL for trusted statements:"}]},{"code":["try await database.execute {","    \"INSERT INTO users(id, name) VALUES (1, 'Aisha');\"","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SQLiteKit\/documentation\/SQLiteKit\/PreparedStatement","type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SQLiteKit\/documentation\/SQLiteKit\/SQLParameter","type":"reference"},{"text":" for values that come from users or external systems:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let insert = PreparedStatement(","    query: \"INSERT INTO users(id, name) VALUES (?, ?)\",","    parameters: [.integer(2), .text(\"Omar\")]",")","","_ = try await database.result(parepared: insert)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Query-Rows","level":2,"text":"Query Rows"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Request headers when you want column names:"}]},{"code":["let users = try await database.result(","    header: true,","    parepared: PreparedStatement(","        query: \"SELECT id, name FROM users ORDER BY name\"","    )",")","","for row in users?.records ?? [] {","    print(row)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Close-the-Connection","level":2,"text":"Close the Connection"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SQLiteKit\/documentation\/SQLiteKit\/SQLiteDatabase\/close()"},{"type":"text","text":" when the database is no longer needed:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["await database.close()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Closing finalizes all precompiled statements before closing the SQLite connection."}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SQLiteKit\/documentation\/SQLiteKit"]]},"sections":[],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"SQLiteKit"}],"title":"Getting Started"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Open a SQLite database, declare a schema, insert data, and read rows."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/sqlitekit\/gettingstarted"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SQLiteKit\/documentation\/SQLiteKit\/GettingStarted"},"references":{"doc://SQLiteKit/documentation/SQLiteKit/SQLiteDatabase/schema(mode:entities:)":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"schema(mode:entities:)","url":"\/documentation\/sqlitekit\/sqlitedatabase\/schema(mode:entities:)","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Creates or synchronizes schema entities with the database.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SQLiteKit\/documentation\/SQLiteKit\/SQLiteDatabase\/schema(mode:entities:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"schema","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"mode","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:9SQLiteKit15SchemaMatchModeO","text":"SchemaMatchMode","kind"